1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,915
One wrong curve —
and the steel doesn't fit.

2
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:06,385
So before you cut:
how do you know?

3
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:10,225
NEXUS FABRIC.
Dimensions in.

4
00:00:10,245 --> 00:00:11,701
Flat pattern out.

5
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:15,705
Shells. Cones. Eccentric reducers.
Branches.

6
00:00:15,725 --> 00:00:19,602
Headers with their openings.
Every cut computed, point by point.

7
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:23,275
Then it checks its own work.
Folded back in 3D,

8
00:00:23,295 --> 00:00:25,479
both edges must be one curve.

9
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:29,300
The DXF is written,
read back, and compared.

10
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:32,075
Underneath runs AMOEBA.

11
00:00:32,095 --> 00:00:35,215
Every value and every step
is recorded and linked.

12
00:00:35,235 --> 00:00:36,340
Change one number —

13
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:39,435
and everything that depended
on it is flagged for review.

14
00:00:39,485 --> 00:00:41,841
Replay a job, and it must match.

15
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:44,815
What it cannot confirm,
it shows. The result stays:

16
00:00:44,835 --> 00:00:46,139
review required.

17
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:49,694
In English and Japanese.
And it runs fully offline.

18
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:53,247
NEXUS FABRIC.
Engineering, reimagined.

